From e115c24ca76cc26bb85f47e837e162698953fdbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawson Horvath <horvath.dawson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:41:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core): apply feature state to a tile once, then only
 changes

SourceFeatureState::coalesceChanges runs every frame and, since #3406,
merged the whole stored state into the frame's changes and gave it to
every rendered tile, so every frame re-evaluated the feature-state paint
of every tile for every id ever set.

Keep a version, bumped in a frame with changes. A tile records the
version its buckets hold (reset by GeometryTile::onLayout). A tile one
version behind gets this frame's changes; a tile with new buckets, or
one that missed a version, gets the whole state; an up-to-date tile gets
nothing. A removal now merges into the same frame's changes instead of
replacing that source layer's changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
